+# Docs route
+
+Each `nsc-*.md` file is one research strand. Read that file for its
+assumptions, domain, and what it does not claim. This index does not merge
+those strands into one settled theory.
+
+| Question | Page |
+|---|---|
+| What the calculations currently show | [current-result.md](current-result.md) |
+| How to regenerate records | [reproducing.md](reproducing.md) |
+| Prior art versus the open claim | [prior-art-and-open-claim.md](prior-art-and-open-claim.md) |
+| 10 September 2026 development record | [development-update-2026-09-10.md](development-update-2026-09-10.md) |
+| Declared action scope | [nsc-declared-action-scope.md](nsc-declared-action-scope.md) |
+| Reuse before new compute | [nsc-prior-art-reuse.md](nsc-prior-art-reuse.md) |
+
+Other `nsc-*.md` names are the strand list. A shared filename prefix is only
+a finding aid.
+
+## Relationship to the laboratory repository
+
+This checkout is an independent Git repository, not a linked worktree of the
+BlackHoles-Infinity laboratory history. When this route was written, 111
+shared `docs/*.md` names were byte-identical with that repository's `docs/`
+copies. Two shared names differed: `current-result.md` and `reproducing.md`.
+
+This repository has no `lab/` tree. The laboratory repository additionally
+carries `instructions.md`, `papers.md`, `repository-consolidation.md`,
+`local-gate-draft.md`, `PLAN.md`, `nsc-nested-qualities.md`, and
+`nsc-local-observer-correspondence.md`, plus a large `lab/docs/` set.
+Identical bytes are imported publication copies of one strand, not a second
+result. The two divergent files are separate texts.
+
+There is no `PLAN.md` here. Historical task plans are not authority in this
+repository. The current frontier is [current-result.md](current-result.md).
